.TH "AUDIODATA.COPYTO" "3JS" "May 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
AudioData.copyTo \- AudioData: copyTo() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]copyTo()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]AudioData\f[R]
interface copies a plane of an \f[CR]AudioData\f[R] object to a
destination buffer.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
copyTo(destination, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]destination\f[R]
An \f[CR]ArrayBuffer\f[R], a \f[CR]TypedArray\f[R], or a
\f[CR]DataView\f[R] to copy the plane to.
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R]
An object containing the following:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]planeIndex\f[R]
The index of the plane to copy from.
.TP
\f[B]frameOffset\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer giving the offset of the first frame to copy within the
plane.
Defaults to \f[CR]0\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]frameCount\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer giving the number of frames to copy.
If omitted, all frames from \f[CR]frameOffset\f[R] to the end of the
plane are copied.
.TP
\f[B]format\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string indicating the audio format that the source samples should be
converted to when copied to the destination.
This can be any of the values: \f[CR]\(dqu8\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqs16\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqs32\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqf32\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqu8\-planar\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqs16\-planar\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqs32\-planar\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqf32\-planar\(dq\f[R] (see
\f[CR]AudioData.format\f[R] for more information).
Note that \f[CR]\(dqf32\-planar\(dq\f[R] must be supported.
If omitted, the samples are copied in the \f[CR]AudioData\f[R]\(cqs own
format.
.RE
.SS Return value
Undefined.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the \f[CR]AudioData\f[R] object has been transferred.
.TP
\f[B]RangeError\f[R]
Thrown if one of the following conditions is met:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The length of the sample is longer than the destination length.
.IP \(bu 2
The format of the \f[CR]AudioData\f[R] object describes a planar format,
but \f[CR]options.planeIndex\f[R] is outside of the number of planes
available.
.IP \(bu 2
The format of the \f[CR]AudioData\f[R] object describes an interleaved
format, but \f[CR]options.planeIndex\f[R] is greater than \f[CR]0\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]NotSupportedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the specified \f[CR]format\f[R] to convert the data to is not
supported.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following example copies the plane at index \f[CR]1\f[R] to a
destination buffer.
.IP
.EX
AudioData.copyTo(AudioBuffer, { planeIndex: 1 });
.EE
